    "detailed_description": "Rules are simple: <br />\r\nIf you observe an anomaly, something out-of-place or something not-seen-before, run back to where you started. <br />\r\nOtherwise, keep running. <br />\r\nWhen you reach Exit 11, you\u2019ll manage to escape from this nightmare.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExit Slum 11 is a short &quot;running&quot; simulator inspired by Backrooms and Liminal Spaces.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHowever, we strongly advise that you walk around and observe carefully since in each walkthrough there can be some randomly generated anomaly.<br />\r\nAnd if you fail to spot and anomaly, your dreams of exiting this nightmare will reset back to zero.<br />\r\nThat's why you have to observe carefully, if you miss an anomaly your progress will be lost and you will have to start from the beginning.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe game uses latest version of Unreal Engine 5, so expect some nice visuals.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe game also has some occasional jumpscares, although the purpose of this game is not to scare the player, rather provide some mystery and eerie experience.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe game is designed with realism in mind, so there will be head-bobbing when you are running around.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe options menu has the ability to save your own key-bindings if you prefer something different that W,A,S,D..<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe gameplay time can vary between 10 minutes or even up to 60 minutes depending on your observations skills.",
